      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s oldest courthouse, completed in 1833, still functions today and is the oldest operating courthouse in Tennessee.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlotte%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 1830 tornado destroyed most of downtown Charlotte, scattering the courthouse roof 13 miles away and wiping early records.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlotte%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Charlotte sits on the Highland Rim hills, midway between Dickson and Ashland City, and is crossed by Town Branch, a tributary of the Cumberland River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlotte%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Charlotte’s historic square and homes preserve the town’s 19th‑century stagecoach hub heritage, even as railroads shifted industry to nearby Dickson.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
